  "body": "Auction: 62 Highbrook Drive, East Tamaki on Tuesday 10 November 2026 at 1:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nDevelopers, land bankers, and savvy investors, this property offers rare versatility and unbeatable positioning on a flat 787-square-meter section in one of Bucklands Beach’s most desirable cul-de-sacs. Built with timeless single-level brick and weatherboard, this Home and Income setup provides high-yield dual cash flow alongside exceptional future development potential with all services onsite (subject to Council approval).\r\n\r\nThe primary residence features a spacious four-bedroom layout attached with a two-car garage, paired with a separate two-bedroom minor dwelling complete with its own standalone double garage. This low-maintenance setup is ideal for generating dual rental returns, offsetting holding costs while you explore site potential, or comfortably accommodating multigenerational living.\r\n\r\nPositioned right in the heart of a premier school zone trifecta, your daily routine could not be easier. Children can enjoy a simple four- to five-minute walk to Macleans College and Bucklands Beach Intermediate School, with Macleans Primary School just around the corner.\r\n\r\nThis isn't just a school-zoned property—it's a gold mine and lifestyle balance site. Live your ultimate coastal life with world-class waterfront dining and CBD ferry commutes at Half Moon Bay Marina, relaxing strolls along Bucklands Beach and Eastern Beach, vibrant weekends in Howick Village, and active afternoons at the nearby Lloyd Elsmore Leisure Centre.\r\n\r\nOur vendors are highly motivated to sell, making this a rare chance to land bank, redevelop, or secure top rental yield. \r\n\r\nContact us today to arrange your private viewing or we see you at\r\nour open homes.",
